# Alienation's thing: an alien calls the mothership, and it answers with a companion.
# Performed by tests/screenplays.rs; the reel lands in <target>/tmp/reels/an-alien-calls-home.html

clear
run /spawn merluza "Zed"
run /mutate "Zed" alienation
run /startcallhome
expect GLORP VLERP!
snap Zed calls home, and the mothership descends
tick 30
snap The beam is open on the way down, the companion asleep inside it
tick 40
snap At the floor, the beam holds
tick 65
snap The beam retracts; the companion waits, eyes still shut
tick 30
snap The beam is home: the companion opens its eyes and swims
tick 400
snap A companion has landed: an alien fish, or a cow

clear
run /spawn merluza "Xul"
run /mutate "Xul" alienation
run /startcallhome
run /startcallhome
expect GLORP VLERP!
tick 75
snap Two calls, two UFOs, two companions
tick 400

clear
run /give honey cow
run /mutate "Vaquita" alienation
run /startcallhome
expect GLORP VLERP!
snap An alien cow calls home too
tick 460

clear
run /give blueberry milk
run /give honey milk
run /give matcha milk
run /give milk
run /inventory
expect Blueberry Milk
expect Honey Milk
expect Matcha Milk
snap The three new fishing milks in the inventory
key esc
run /consume blueberry milk
run /consume honey milk
run /consume matcha milk
run /consume milk
expect visual-calculus
expect volition
expect reaction-speed
expect physical-instrument
snap One glass of each: four buffs, one milk apiece
